      "title": "ioctl 0x520a can resubmit the RTP work item after aw_remove cancels it",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "high_static_callpath_and_ordering",
      "condition": "An already-open Richtap file descriptor invokes ioctl 0x520a after the sole cancellation of state+0x648 while aw_remove is continuing to free the RTP buffer/pages. The existing HAP-RICHTAP-02 review confirms misc_deregister does not drain already-open descriptors.",
      "impact": "The resubmitted richtap_rtp_work may execute while state+0x608 or the FIFO pages at state+0x610 are being freed, or after those resources have been released.",
